= Information =

== Overview ==
'''Information''' is a broad concept concerning distinctions, uncertainty reduction, representation, communication, or content.

Different fields use the term differently.

In [[Information theory]], information is quantified probabilistically without requiring semantic meaning.

In computing, information can be represented as data structures, messages, states, or encoded symbols.

In philosophy and linguistics, information can also concern content and meaning.

== Information and data ==
Data are recorded or represented values, symbols, measurements, or observations.

In computing, [[Data structure|data structures]] organize data, but a data structure is not the general concept of data.

Information is not identical to data.

The same data can carry different information for different questions or models.

== Information and meaning ==
Shannon's mathematical theory measures uncertainty and coding properties.

It does not by itself determine whether a message is true, meaningful, useful, or understood.

Therefore:

<pre>
information ≠ meaning by definition
</pre>

== Probabilistic information ==
For an event with probability p, self-information is commonly defined as:

<pre>
I(x) = -log p(x)
</pre>

Less probable events carry more self-information under this measure.

The average self-information of a random variable is [[Entropy|Shannon entropy]].

